@acetcom 
I don't have time ATM to take proper logs so I will close this for now and re-open when I have proper logs to share.

Thank you!

@Sabreu and @bojanHub 

I think I've found the cause of the problem. There were two problems. 

First of all, the 'next' variable is used simultaneously in two for-loops. We need to fix this as below.

```diff
$ diff --git a/src/smf/pfcp-sm.c b/src/smf/pfcp-sm.c
index 348ef3472..9a1f95f8e 100644
--- a/src/smf/pfcp-sm.c
+++ b/src/smf/pfcp-sm.c
@@ -319,13 +319,13 @@ void smf_pfcp_state_associated(ogs_fsm_t *s, smf_event_t *e)
         node = e->pfcp_node;
         ogs_assert(node);
 
-        smf_ue_t *smf_ue = NULL, *next = NULL;;
+        smf_ue_t *smf_ue = NULL, *next_ue = NULL;;
 
-        ogs_list_for_each_safe(&smf_self()->smf_ue_list, next, smf_ue) {
-            smf_sess_t *sess = NULL, *next = NULL;;
+        ogs_list_for_each_safe(&smf_self()->smf_ue_list, next_ue, smf_ue) {
+            smf_sess_t *sess = NULL, *next_sess = NULL;;
             ogs_assert(smf_ue);
 
-            ogs_list_for_each_safe(&smf_ue->sess_list, next, sess) {
+            ogs_list_for_each_safe(&smf_ue->sess_list, next_sess, sess) {
                 ogs_assert(sess);
 
                 if (node == sess->pfcp_node) {
```

Second, the 'node' variable was already deleted in ogs_pfcp_xact_delete() after N4 timeout. Therefore, we should not use 'node' variables passed using message queue.

So, I've fixed it.

Please let me know if you have any other idea.

Thank you so much for raising this issue.
Sukchan
